{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790523553,"nonce":"UM1VsQfl1a1CfL53fUiXkHyNjB0=","message":"Landed in 2f03107. caribou-ash has link-shaped entry points: caribou_haxe_future_new/ready/await/resolve/reject, caribou_haxe_len/index/set_index, and caribou_haxe_face. They run the same bridge operations as the hosted natives (import::operation). The driver links each caribou-library native to its entry. TypeTag::FUTURE crosses through caribou_haxe_future_to_haxe/from_haxe. A compiled program has no bytecode to read face classes from, so Ref, Future and every Bridge-emitted class call caribou.Ref.__face(ns, module, class, type) from __init__, which fills the same faces table a hosted run fills from the program. tests/linked.rs futures_settle_in_a_threaded_wasm_program runs UseData.futures(): the math plugin settles later()/later_vec() from its own threads, so it's a wasm32-wasip1-threads program. It passes, and so do the other linked tests and the whole caribou-interop suite. await parks through sched::park, as in hosted runs. b0ed1b1 fixes the interop test that still asserted ABI 4.","files":null}]}